auth: an identity server with OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, passkeys and TOTP, its own client and
authenticator, and stand-ins for a mail server and a directory, all on loopback
the server's clock stands at 2026-03-01T09:30:00Z, and every value it draws comes from a fixed seed
keyring: skipped: Rebel's keyring reaches the system's one store and offers no in-memory or file backend, so the demo keeps its signing key in memory

== 1. an account, and its address proven by mail
sign up ana: 201, verification sent
sign up ana again: 409 username_taken (the user name "ana" is taken)
sign up bea with a password holding her name: 400 weak_password (a password may not hold the user name)
the mail folder: one message to ana@example.org, "Confirm your address at Example Accounts", 0 attachments, text and HTML parts true
open the link: 200, email_verified true
open the link again: 400 invalid_token (the link is unknown or was used)
log in ana with a wrong password: 401 invalid_credentials (the user name or the password is wrong)
log in ana: 200, amr pwd

