confirm with the app's code of 09:30:00: 200
log out, then log in ana with her password alone: 401 totp_required (the account asks a TOTP code too)
log in with the code just used: 401 invalid_totp (the code was used already)
log in with the app's next code, 09:30:30: 200, amr pwd otp

== 3. a passkey, and a login without a password
registration options: 200, rp localhost, attestation direct
register the authenticator's credential: 200, attestation certified by Heroes Demo Authenticator Root
register the same response again: 400 invalid_registration (no registration was begun in this session)
log in by the passkey: 200, ana, amr hwk user, counter 1
the same assertion against a new challenge: 401 invalid_assertion (the client data's challenge is not the one sent)

== 4. OpenID Connect: the authorization code with PKCE
discovery: issuer holds true, PKCE S256, ID tokens ES256, iss on redirects true
JWK set: 1 key, EC P-256, ES256, its id the key's thumbprint
authorize: 302 to https://portal.example.org/callback, code, state and iss hold
exchange the code: Bearer, refresh token true, ID token true, scopes openid profile email offline_access
verify the ID token: ES256 signature, iss, aud, nonce, exp and at_hash hold
    sub 019ca8bb-b5c0-794b-b5a6-ef13ec04c318, aud portal, amr hwk user, auth_time 1772357400
    preferred_username ana, email ana@example.org, email_verified true
userinfo: sub name preferred_username email email_verified
exchange the same code again: refused, failed: the server answered 400 invalid_grant: the authorization code is unknown or was used
authorize: 302 to https://portal.example.org/callback, code, state and iss hold
exchange a new code with another verifier: refused, failed: the server answered 400 invalid_grant: the code verifier does not answer the challenge
refresh: a new access token true, the refresh token rotated true
refresh with the first refresh token again: refused, failed: the server answered 400 invalid_grant: the refresh token was used already: its family is revoked
introspect the newest refresh token: active false, its family revoked by the replay
authorize: 302 to https://portal.example.org/callback, code, state and iss hold
a third login, its refresh token introspected: active true, sub true, scopes openid profile email offline_access
revoke it (RFC 7009), then introspect: active false
introspect its access token: active true, client portal

== 5. a service account: SCRAM-SHA-256 over HTTP
log in with a wrong password: refused, 401 invalid_client (the proof of "directory-sync" does not hold)
first round trip: 401 with a sid and the server's first message, 4096 iterations
second round trip: 200, the server's signature verified, scopes directory:import users:read

